WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.180
FedRAMP emphasizes continuous monitoring rather than one-time assessment.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.590
Cloud environments change, vulnerabilities appear, configurations evolve, users change,

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:12.425
incidents occur, and services continue to develop after authorization.

00:00:12.425 --> 00:00:16.790
Continuous monitoring helps organizations maintain visibility into security controls,

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:21.610
vulnerabilities, system changes, operational risks, and remediation activities over time.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:25.200
Monitoring may include vulnerability scanning, configuration management,

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.300
incident reporting, plan of action updates, control status reporting, change tracking,

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.310
and review of security-relevant events.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.230
The goal is not to collect information for its own sake.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.160
Monitoring should help agencies, providers,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.730
and stakeholders understand whether the cloud service continues to operate within an

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.310
acceptable risk posture.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.720
Continuous monitoring also supports accountability.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.520
If a control weakens, a vulnerability remains open,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.720
or a system change affects the security boundary,

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.620
decision makers need current information.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.720
For technical teams, continuous monitoring connects FedRAMP to daily operations.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.225
Patch management, logging, alerting, change control, vulnerability remediation,

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.940
incident response, and configuration review all contribute to the security picture.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.394
The practical takeaway is that FedRAMP is ongoing.

00:01:05.394 --> 00:01:07.215
Authorization is not the end of the work;

00:01:07.215 --> 00:01:10.945
it is part of a lifecycle that depends on sustained visibility and management.

00:01:10.945 --> 00:01:14.390
Continuous monitoring also supports better conversations with agencies.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:17.475
Current information about vulnerabilities, changes, incidents,

00:01:17.475 --> 00:01:21.440
and remediation gives stakeholders a clearer view of whether the service remains within

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.865
expected risk boundaries.

00:01:22.865 --> 00:01:26.880
For program teams, this means monitoring evidence should be reliable and repeatable.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.130
The organization needs processes that can produce current information without rebuilding

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.630
the entire security story from scratch each month.
